    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42188" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐργᾰτ-ίνης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐργάτης</span>
			, esp. <i>husbandman,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				10.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.376
			</span></i> (pl.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἄνδρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					21.3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.58
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦς ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.663
				</span></i>
			 (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.228
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Adaeus</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. gen., <i>making</i> a thing or
				<i>practising</i> an art, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλιτος ὁ χρυσὸς ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.239
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπριδος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				274
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.).</div>
